clk: qcom: camcc-sm8450: park the RCGs on XO while disabled

From the Galaxy Tab S8+ port (https://github.com/aaronsb/sm-x800-linux,
camcc-sm8450-shared-rcg.patch, GPL-2.0-only). With clk_rcg2_ops the camera
RCGs keep selecting PLL0/PLL3 after a session while those PLLs are off; the
next TITAN_TOP/IFE GDSC power-up then waits for clocks that never toggle
and every later camera session fails until reboot. camcc-sm8550/8650 use
clk_rcg2_shared_ops for this reason; do the same here.

diff --git a/drivers/clk/qcom/camcc-sm8450.c b/drivers/clk/qcom/camcc-sm8450.c
index 4dd8be8cc..7f1304ee6 100644
